<h1>Mike Vick</h1>
<p>Governor &amp; Lieutenant Governor, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: American Solidarity Party. Declared write-in.</p>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.votevickusa.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (votevickusa.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. Running with Gary Pierce, a Navy veteran, addiction counselor, and ordained minister. Vick calls his campaign a &quot;pro-life for the whole life&quot; alternative and proposes shifting corporate subsidies toward small family businesses, local farms, and worker-owned co-ops, repairing existing roads before building new highways, and using citizen assemblies chosen by lottery to take on issues like pensions.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Former reporter for Catholic San Francisco and SEIU organizer who chairs the party&#39;s Illinois affiliate; he was the party&#39;s endorsed candidate for Congress in Illinois&#39;s 2nd District in 2024 and hosts the Unorthodoxing podcast.</p>
